{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089449-quick-question-on-spellcasting-2e","id":1089449,"title":"Quick question on spellcasting (2e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T16:21:04-07:00","id":1089449,"title":"Quick question on spellcasting (2e)","content":"So, in 1e success were added to primary factor. If am reading correctly now the spell's arcana is what gets added to the primary factor (if the caster wants) and success are there just to check if spell works or not (except that the spell hold some special rule for successes).<br /> <br /> Did i got that right?<br /> <br /> Also, i notice attack spells dont have a withstood entrance. So this means that the target cannot resist and receive full damage? (this seems weird, i must be getting it wrong).<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13406,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13406-iasblas","user":"IASBLAS","date":". 05-07-2017, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13406-iasblas","name":"IASBLAS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:25:06-07:00","id":1089454,"title":"","content":"Yep, base primary spell factor is the casters spell arcana - 1, every -2 dice increases the spell factor by +1, you only need 1 success to cast the spell. All other spell factors are 1, and you can take penalties on those too.<br /> <br /> You can take combined penalties up to -5 (chance dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:29:41-07:00","id":1089456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IASBLAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089449-quick-question-on-spellcasting-2e#post1089449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(except that the spell hold some special rule for successes)</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell doesn't have special rules for successes, but there are some extra benefits to casting a spell and getting an Exceptional Success. These are general benefits though and not relevant to what spell you're casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:30:20-07:00","id":1089459,"title":"","content":"Correct. Number of successes only matter when you succeed exceptionally, in that getting five or more allows the player to choose an extra thing that happens from the list on p. 115. You move primary factor up its chart (if desired) by Arcana dots minus 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:44:16-07:00","id":1089467,"title":"","content":"Attack spells don't use Withstand because they're up against the health track. Most people have Withstand ratings around 2 and health around 7. Transforming a person into a frog requires around 3 Potency while filling an average health track would require more than twice that Potency.<br /> Of course, it means that damage spells are the only spells that can whittle down the subject instead of being an on/off type deal as with regular Withstand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:57:09-07:00","id":1089471,"title":"","content":"Ok. Thanks for quick responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13406-iasblas","name":"IASBLAS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:03:05-07:00","id":1089473,"title":"","content":"An example starting mage with Gnosis 3 and a Arcana at 3 can quite easily do 7 bashing via magic if built right. Take the fraying spell as a rote, have a good rote skill and your looking at Gnosis 3 + Arcana 3 + 4 Mudra rote (Space 3's Warp uses athlethics, so athletics 4 is always useful anyways for defense, if you align up to get a order bonus another +1). Your base potency is 3 so you can take a -8 to pump up its potency/damage to 7. Being a rote you get 3 free reaches, you can use one for instant casting, one for advanced scale and choose 5 people, and 1 for um.<br /> <br /> This leaves you with 2 dice which if you roll a success you do 7 bashing to 5 people. Spend willpower and thats 5 dice, not to shabby.<br /> <br /> Since you have space you can ritually cast and sympathetically cast this and add extra time factors giving another +5 dice and another yantra of say +2 for +7 dice (9 dice before willpower), you then can take another -4 for another +2 potency, a -2 for duration (spending that other reach on advanced duration) which makes the spell take 6 hours to cast and do 9 bashing every 1 hour with 3 dice. You'd need to get a good strong connection to them tho as the sympathetic damage spells are withstood by sympathy, so say you had a strong connection without knowing the name that'd be a withstand of 2 (1 for the conenction +1 for not knowing their name). So the spell should do 7 bashing per hour for one day. (people heal what 4 bashing per hour, so 3 bashing an hour really).<br /> <br /> Once you get to space 4 you can start smacking people with 7 agg too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-07-2017, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}